{"id":"s3.1.7","slug":"log-rules","title":"Log Rules","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Logarithm problems test your knowledge of fundamental log properties:</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li><strong>Definition:</strong> $\\log_a b = x \\iff a^x = b$</li><li><strong>Power Rule:</strong> $\\log_a (b^n) = n \\log_a b$</li><li><strong>Addition/Subtraction:</strong> $\\log_a b + \\log_a c = \\log_a(bc)$ and $\\log_a b - \\log_a c = \\log_a(b/c)$</li><li><strong>Change of Base:</strong> $\\log_a b = \\frac{\\log_c b}{\\log_c a}$</li></ul><p>Approximations are also common: $\\log_{10} 2 \\approx 0.3$, $\\log_{10} 5 \\approx 0.7$, $\\ln 2 \\approx 0.7$, $\\ln 10 \\approx 2.3$.</p>","summary":"Logarithm problems test your knowledge of fundamental log properties: Definition: Power Rule: Addition/Subtraction: and Change of Base: Approximations are also common: , , , .","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem that requires applying one of the basic logarithm rules.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"If $-2 \\log_3 x = 4$, x =","answer":"1/9","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","logs-exponents"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $\\log_{12} 2 + \\log_{12} 8 + \\log_{12} 9$.","answer":"2","kind":"exact","tags":["logs-exponents"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $\\log_3 40 - \\log_3 8 + \\log_3 1.8$.","answer":"2","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","logs-exponents"]},{"id":4,"text":"If $\\log_x 216 = 3$, x =","answer":"6","kind":"exact","tags":["logs-exponents"]},{"id":5,"text":"If $f(x) = \\log_3 x - 4$, $f(3) =$","answer":"-3","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","functions","logs-exponents"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $\\log_8 16$.","answer":"4/3","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","logs-exponents"]},{"id":7,"text":"If $\\log_3 x = 4$, $\\sqrt{x} =$","answer":"9","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","logs-exponents"]},{"id":8,"text":"If $\\log_x 343 = 3$, x =","answer":"7","kind":"exact","tags":["logs-exponents"]},{"id":9,"text":"If log .25 = 3, then log 4 =","answer":"-3","kind":"exact","tags":["arithm